# =============================================================================
# Git Ignore Configuration
# =============================================================================
# Files and directories that should not be committed to version control.
#
# To add project-specific ignores without modifying this file:
#   1. Create .git/info/exclude (local only, not committed)
#   2. Or add to ~/.config/git/ignore (global)
#
# Note: gitignore only treats `#` as a comment when it starts the line.
# Inline comments after a pattern are interpreted as part of the pattern.
# =============================================================================

# --- Rust Build Artifacts ---
# Backup files from rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk
# Windows debug symbols
*.pdb
target/
# sccache cache directory (see .envrc)
.sccache/

# bin/bootstrap's project-local tool installs (ast-grep, cargo-dylint,
# dylint-link) via `cargo install --root ./.cargo` — see .envrc. Ignoring
# specific entries, not the whole .cargo/ directory, so a future root-level
# .cargo/config.toml (this workspace already has one under
# .lints/rust-quality-dylint/) stays trackable.
/.cargo/bin/
/.cargo/.crates.toml
/.cargo/.crates2.json

# Cargo.lock is tracked because this workspace contains binary services.
# For library-only workspaces, uncomment to exclude it:
# Cargo.lock

# --- macOS ---
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Icon
._*
*.icloud

# --- Environment & Secrets ---
# Environment variables (may contain secrets)
.env
# Local overrides
.env.local
# .envrc is intentionally tracked (no secrets, just PATH setup)
# direnv cache
.direnv

# --- Security/Credentials (NEVER commit these) ---
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.cer
*.der
*.priv
*.p12
*.pfx

# --- IDE/Editor ---
# JetBrains IDEs
.idea/
# VS Code (uncomment to track shared settings)
.vscode/
# Vim swap files
*.swp
*.swo
# Backup files
*~

# --- Testing & Coverage ---
# Coverage reports already live under target/ (gitignored above)
# Raw coverage data
*.profraw
# Processed coverage data
*.profdata

# --- Documentation ---
# Ignore scratch/generated markdown; allowlist standard project docs
**/*.md
!**/README*.md
!**/TODO.md
!**/AGENTS.md
# Generated by git-cliff from conventional commits at each release — a
# durable, versioned artifact, not scratch. Anchored for the same
# `core.ignorecase` reason as AUDIT-*/TICKET-*/UI-* below.
!/CHANGELOG.md
!**/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md
# docs/plans/ and docs/specs/ are per-session scratch (design docs and plans
# generated while working, not durable project docs), so they stay under the
# blanket **/*.md ignore above. Each directory keeps a tracked .gitkeep so the
# folder itself still exists in a fresh clone.
# Audit reports at the repository root. A findings document whose
# recommendations nobody can diff is not a finding, it is a note — and this one
# was silently ignored for a whole commit before anybody noticed it was missing
# from the tree.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash on purpose. Unanchored, git matches the pattern
# at every level, and `core.ignorecase` (on by default on macOS) makes it match
# lowercase too — so `!AUDIT-*.md` also un-ignored the agents' scratch
# `.strip-reports/audit-*.md` working notes.
!/AUDIT-*.md
# Deferred-work tickets at the repository root. The point of one is that it
# outlives the session that wrote it and reaches whoever picks the work up, so
# it has to be in the tree — an untracked ticket is a note to yourself.
#
# Unlike `AUDIT-*` below, these are NOT re-ignored: an audit is a snapshot whose
# line references rot, while a ticket records a decision and what it would take
# to revisit it.
#
# Anchored for the same `core.ignorecase` reason as the line above.
!/TICKET-*.md
# Integration handovers at the repository root, by the same argument: these are
# the contract another team builds against, so a change to one has to show up
# in a diff. Anchored for the same `core.ignorecase` reason as the line above.
!/UI-*.md
# tests/access/REPORT.md is a generated artifact whose diff IS the review
# signal (denial cells flipping to visible), so it must be committable.
!tests/access/REPORT.md

# --- Claude Code ---
# Track .claude/ contents (slash commands, etc.) but exclude per-user state
!.claude
!.claude/**/*.md
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees

# Hook reports (transient)
.claude/hooks/.last-*.txt

# Scheduled-task session lock (transient runtime state)
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# ignore obsidian
.obsidian

# Local large fixture files for manual/local testing — not for the repo.
TEST_DATA/


.agents/

AUDIT-*
